# Echoes of the Hollow Realm Rule Book

## Canon and Tone
- Preserve dark fantasy + time-loop identity: "Die, learn, return... break the cycle."
- Keep writing concise, atmospheric, and choice-driven; avoid comedy that breaks immersion.
- Treat The Keeper as morally ambiguous, never purely good or evil.

## Core Gameplay Pillars
- Every death must teach something and alter the next loop (state, options, dialogue, or difficulty).
- Choices must have meaningful trade-offs (power vs cost, safety vs lore, mercy vs corruption).
- Combat remains turn-based, readable, and text-first; effects support clarity, not clutter.

## Progression and Balance
- Keep progression steady: visible gains each loop without trivializing elites/bosses.
- SOUL, LUCK, and Soul Burst should influence outcomes but never invalidate basic attack/defend play.
- Rare/relic items may be strong, but should include explicit drawbacks or conditions.

## UI and UX Style
- Use pixel font and glassmorphism-dark visual language consistently.
- Prioritize readability over visual effects (high contrast, restrained animation, low audio mix).
- New micro-interactions must be subtle and performant on mobile and web.

## Content and Naming Conventions
- Name content with Hollow Realm vocabulary (Echo, Hollow, Soul, Rift, Keeper, Loop, Abyss, Ruins).
- Keep enemy tiers explicit: common, elite, boss.
- Preserve asset naming discipline (snake_case file names; deterministic IDs for items/enemies/events).

## Implementation Guardrails
- Favor modular services for combat, events, audio, and progression logic.
- Avoid hidden side effects: state transitions should be explicit in provider/service methods.
- Add/adjust logs whenever gameplay behavior changes so player feedback stays transparent.
